<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Church, People of God" cic="CCC 751-870" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does the word &laquo;Church&raquo; (from the Greek <em>ekklesía</em>) mean?</li>
<li>What are the four marks of the Church that we profess in the Creed?</li>
<li>What does it mean that the Church is &laquo;apostolic&raquo;?</li>
<li>What image does Saint Paul use to speak of the Church as unity in diversity?</li>
<li>Who is the successor of Saint Peter and what is his role in the Church?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Describe an experience in which you felt the Church was truly a community, a family. What happened? How did you feel?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">It could be a retreat, a special Mass, a youth group, service to the poor, or simply a deep conversation with someone from your parish.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Is there something about the Church that causes you difficulty, confusion, or even annoyance? How do you handle it?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">We all have something: the hierarchy, some difficult teachings, the failings of Christians. It is normal. What matters is how you process it.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. What gifts or talents do you believe God has given you to put at the service of the Church? Are you using them?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">All the baptized have something to offer: time, knowledge, creativity, hospitality, faith, prayer. What can you give?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. The Church is holy but made up of sinners. How do you live that tension in your own life?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Do your own falls discourage you? Or do you learn to receive God&rsquo;s mercy and move forward?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. How can you be a better member of the Body of Christ this week?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think of a concrete action: help at your parish, reconcile with someone, pray for the Pope, invite someone to Mass, read a Church document.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Research your parish</h4>
<p>Find out when your parish was founded, who its patron saint is, what groups or ministries exist. If possible, interview the pastor or a layperson who has been there a long time. Write a short history of your parish.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Read Acts 2:42-47 and compare with your parish</h4>
<p>This passage describes the life of the first Christian community. Read the text and make a list of the characteristics of that community. Then, next to each one, write how it is lived (or could be lived) in your parish.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Write a letter to a persecuted Christian</h4>
<p>In many places around the world, Christians are persecuted for their faith. Learn about the situation of the Church in a country where being a Christian is dangerous (Syria, Nigeria, North Korea, India). Write a brief letter expressing your solidarity and your prayer.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;But you are a chosen race, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, God&rsquo;s own people, that you may declare the wonderful deeds of him who called you out of darkness into his marvelous light.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; 1 Peter 2:9</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord Jesus Christ,<br />
you who called the Apostles<br />
and built your Church upon Peter,<br />
thank you for making me a member of your Body.<br />
Help me to love her as you love her,<br />
to serve her with my gifts,<br />
not to be scandalized by her wounds<br />
but to be part of her healing.<br />
May I be a living stone in your Church,<br />
and may many come to know your love through my life.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

